<div class="contextual">
  <%= link_to reporter_dashboard_icon('download', l(:label_reporter_template_export)),
              export_project_reporter_template_path(@project, @template),
              class: 'icon icon-download' %>
</div>

<h2><%= l(:label_reporter_template) %>: <%= @template.name %></h2>

<%= labelled_form_for :template, @template,
                      url: project_reporter_template_path(@project, @template),
                      html: { method: :patch, id: 'reporter-template-form' } do |f| %>
  <%= render partial: 'form', locals: { f: f } %>
  <p>
    <%= submit_tag l(:button_save) %>
    <%#
      PREVIEW IS A SEPARATE SUBMIT ON THE SAME FORM, so it carries the editor's unsaved
      content — which is the only thing that makes it a preview rather than a second way
      of opening the report.

      `formmethod: 'post'` changes the HTTP verb and NOT the form body, and this form's
      body contains Rails' hidden `_method=patch`. `Rack::MethodOverride` reads that field
      and rewrites the request to PATCH before it reaches the router, so the preview route
      accepts both verbs — see the comment on it in `config/routes.rb`. Getting this wrong
      is a 404 on every press, which is what the first version of this did.
    %>
    <%= submit_tag l(:label_preview),
                   name: 'preview',
                   formaction: preview_project_reporter_template_path(@project, @template),
                   formmethod: 'post' %>
    <%= link_to l(:button_cancel), project_reporter_templates_path(@project) %>
  </p>
<% end %>
